  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 115 PM Saturday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... The persistent pattern of dry and largely \nseasonable weather will continue through next week. \n\nThe mid and upper level weather pattern will feature high amplitude \nupper level ridge extending from the western Gulf north into the \nwestern Great Lakes with a general northerly flow across the \nCarolinas through Monday. The ridge will weaken and flatten as it \nslowly shifts east reaching the eastern U.S. coast by early in the \nweekend. Moisture-starved disturbances will move near or across our \narea early Sunday morning and Wednesday night with little impact. \n\nAt the surface, high pressure centered over New England today will \nshift south into the mid Atlantic for Sunday and Monday. A \nreinforcing Canadian high will build into the region for Wednesday \nand Thursday with potentially another surface high extending into \nour region for Saturday. \n\nIt's worth noting that as the ridge flattens and shifts east late \nin the week/weekend and the flow becomes more westerly and even \nsouthwesterly, deep layer moisture will increase somewhat resulting \nin more clouds. There will also be the need to consider limited \nnon-zero rain chances late next weekend into early next week.",
